#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# hypergeometric_2f1

#% text
# `hypergeometric_2f1(a, b, c, z)` gives the Gauss hypergeometric function `2F1(a, b; c; z)`.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# The series is the sum of `(a)_k*(b)_k/(c)_k*z^k/k!` (DLMF 15.2.1), convergent for `abs(z) < 1`; the function is continued analytically with a branch cut on `z > 1`.

#% item
# A non-positive integer `a` or `b` makes the series terminate. Many parameter sets reduce to elementary functions.

#% item
# Machine numbers, balls and complex numbers give numerical values. `hypergeometric_2f1` is listable.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
hypergeometric_2f1(1, 1, 2, 0.5)
#% output
#= 1.3862943611198906

#% cell
hypergeometric_2f1(0.5, 0.5, 1.5, 0.25)
#% output
#= 1.0471975511965979

#% cell
hypergeometric_2f1(-2, 1.5, 2.5, 0.7)
#% output
#= 0.37000000000000005

#% cell
n(hypergeometric_2f1(1/3, 2/3, 3/2, 1/4), 30)
#% output
#= 1.0418890660015820931102997606158888

#% subsection
# Scope

#% text
# Outside the unit disc:

#% cell
hypergeometric_2f1(0.5, 1.0, 2.0, -5.0)
#% output
#= 0.5797958971132713

#% text
# A complex argument:

#% cell
hypergeometric_2f1(1.0, 2.0, 3.0, 0.5*im)
#% output
#= 0.8925742052568391 + 0.29081912799355114im

#% subsection
# Properties and relations

#% text
# `2F1(1, 1; 2; z)` is `-log(1 - z)/z`:

#% cell
hypergeometric_2f1(1, 1, 2, 0.3) + log(0.7)/0.3
#% output
#= -4.440892098500626e-16

#% text
# Gauss's sum at `z = 1`:

#% cell
hypergeometric_2f1(0.5, 0.25, 2.0, 1.0) - gamma(2.0)*gamma(1.25)/(gamma(1.5)*gamma(1.75))
#% output
#= 2.220446049250313e-16

#% subsection
# Possible issues

#% text
# Symbolic arguments stay unevaluated, also when the series terminates:

#% cell
hypergeometric_2f1(-2, b, c, z)
#% output
#= 1 - 2*b*z/c + b*(1 + b)*z^2/(c*(1 + c))

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `hypergeometric_1f1`, `hypergeometric_pfq`, `hypergeometric_0f1`, `pochhammer`
